WEBVTT

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.180
It's too cruel for a kid like this.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.300
Dammit, dammit!

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.850
If my powers were
greater, this wouldn't

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.080
have happened to Hibiki and Nitta!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.040
Greater power...

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.570
Well? How's he been doing?

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.170
Not good. Unconscious the whole time.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.200
Hibiki.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.490
Hey, you!

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.180
I know you're depressed and all,
but it's not like it's your fault!

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.290
You gotta stop burdening
yourself like this.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.330
It wouldn't make HIM happy, either.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.840
I'm sorry. You're right.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.030
Everyone has it rough.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.220
It's tough for all of us.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.700
Thank you.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.120
He's alive. He'll be fine.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.820
You should rest.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.520
We'll take care of things somehow.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.200
So Hibiki won't come back here?

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.290
It's not so unexpected.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.970
Alcor.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.830
Ah. It's you two.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.920
How long do you intend to play
around with these humans?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.780
This was supposed to
be the humans' trial.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.650
Yes, you're right.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.790
That's precisely it, but...

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:42.810
It seems that I've grown to like them.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.620
"Like"? I don't understand the concept.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.830
I've wanted to know about
this "Total Void" that

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.330
will visit the humans
when they've lost hope.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.320
That's too bad.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.030
A difference of opinion,
eh? Interesting.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.300
Right now, THIS is how
strongly I feel...

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.460
About overcoming Polaris' natural
order, seeing if miracles

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.190
and hope truly exist.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.410
Nothing but a broken cog, huh?

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.220
What do YOU think?

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.870
You gotta be kidding! I obey you.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.530
I see.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.140
Uh, well then.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.980
Grown to like them, eh?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.500
I do think I've become strange.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.880
Well, I should go, too.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.440
Because I have to observe...

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:59.540
This world's fate, which
I have brought forth.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.540
Even if it's the end of all.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:07.830
Now then...

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.460
It's done.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.770
This new model is based
on the Nicaea app.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:17.360
Which, I hate to say, is far
more powerful than JP's app.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.600
I went ahead and ported everything
from the old devices.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.410
Tomorrow is the final battle.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.700
It's our time.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.060
Sakotchi, you should rest, too.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.360
Fumi. Thank you for all you've done.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.420
Cut that out.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.970
You can be hard on yourself, but
I did this 'cause I liked it.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.420
Good night.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.220
Good night.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:53.750
Good morning!

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.520
How's Hibiki?

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:58.080
Not yet, huh?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.460
He should just rest today.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:04.740
Yup. While he's sleeping,
we'll settle things.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:07.600
I don't wanna push anything more on him.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:09.750
That's right.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.790
Hibiki's done more than enough.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.000
We can't cause him any more pain.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.230
Ah, jeez!

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.300
There are no demons
stronger than Lorelei.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:25.270
I can't even get any demons
stronger than Heget.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:30.210
Well, this thing's limit is
set by the user's ability.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.370
So, my abilities are weak?!

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.610
You've done well, makin'
it unharmed all this way.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.440
You're lucky your demon is strong.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.360
Well, if it comes down to it,
I'll protect ya with my Lorelei.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.780
Dammit!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.370
Chawanmushi!

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.590
Huh? That's part of our rations?!

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:53.250
I made it.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.710
And I helped.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.230
Oh!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.550
Feelin' better, huh?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:03.970
It's delicious.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.090
Right?

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.470
Jungo used to work at a restaurant.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.600
I'm still learning.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.560
Huh.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.560
I wondered what kinda guy you were.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.040
So you ain't a pimp, huh?

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.020
I thought you were somebody scary.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.520
I am not scary.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.820
Well, if you say nothing,

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.070
people won't know what
kinda person you are.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:25.320
Speaking of, we haven't proper
introduced ourselves, have we?

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.120
Oh, you're right.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.890
I'm Airi Ban. I'm a
high-school freshman.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.340
I'm Jungo Torii. An apprentice.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.420
Hinako Kujo. I'm a Japanese
dance choreographer.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.560
I'm Daichi Shijima.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.150
A third-year in high school.
Taking my college exams.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.910
I'm Io Nitta. Also a third-year.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.520
This is kinda weird!

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:53.560
It's funny!

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.020
Wow, you're two years older, huh?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.850
You'd better respect your elders!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.270
Jeez, here we go.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.460
Ah, she's gonna cry again!

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.940
Nitta, what's up?

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.850
I'm just happy for some reason.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.070
I'm sorry.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.050
Look, apologies are forbidden!

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.870
Thank you, Miss Ban.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.710
Just call me Airi... Miss Nitta.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.540
You can call me "Io."

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.780
You're a good girl.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.340
Okay, everyone!

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.360
Let's celebrate by exchanging e-mails!

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.720
What, now?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.510
Hey, where's the harm?

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.140
I ain't doing some singles' meetup.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.720
What d'you mean, "celebrate"?

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.020
Well, it's just... I mean,
we've all become friends.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.850
Friends. That's nice.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.730
Okay, let's use the IR function.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:49.590
A friend's dead face clip has arrived!

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.840
All of us? What the heck?

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:10.220
This is... It can't happen!

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:11.890
How terrible.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.310
It's here.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:20.120
The last one.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:25.320
The last Septentrion.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.200
Sapporo, please come in! Please come in!

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.120
With a single attack...

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.680
It's the final trial.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.530
BeneTnasch readings are
gone! It's transported!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.550
The trait of the final Septentrion...

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.840
It's all-powerful.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.200
The strongest of our enemies,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.530
with all the abilities of
the prior Septentriones.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.040
You could call it the chief, huh?

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.110
Osaka Branch is silent.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.440
The barrier's destroyed!

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.000
Western Japan is being eroded.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.590
For JP's  bases to be
directly crushed...

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:13.280
Even maintaining the
barriers was for nothing.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.890
We of JP's are criminals.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.240
We've withheld the truth,
turned our back on others,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.210
even used the powers of demons,

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.290
all to survive up till this day...

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:27.690
We MUST win, no matter what!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.570
Ma'am!

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.860
And you all.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.110
You can hate me if you like.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.740
But we need your powers, too.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.430
B-But the dead face--

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.020
We'll do it!

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.910
The dead face clips can be beaten!

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.850
A dead face clip?

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:46.930
I see.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.710
Nagoya Branch has gone silent!

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:54.050
Those with power must fulfill
their responsibilities.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.700
Such is the trial imposed
upon the gifted ones.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.310
All hands, move out!

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.450
You ain't gotta tell us.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:05.360
We're goin' not 'cause you ordered
it, but 'cause we choose to!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:07.860
Sir.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.650
What about you?

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.360
Of course.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.740
Attack the enemy at full force.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.220
We will... destroy God.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.440
Hibiki, you're such a good boy.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.720
It really is a help.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.340
Don't make more work for your mom.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:36.160
Yes, Father. Mother.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.490
Stop it, you all!

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:42.500
Let's go.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.350
Nerd! Blegh!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.300
If you help, you'll be
bullied too, Daichi.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:52.230
Huh? Hibiki, you did
nothing wrong, right?

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.570
It's fine. I'll beat up those guys!

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.180
Awesome!

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.550
Hibiki, the way you teach,

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:04.340
I understand it more than the teacher!

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:07.020
You just don't concentrate
in class, do you?

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:13.990
I'm home.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.820
Hibiki, you've been
coming home late a lot.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.350
It's all right. I'm just taking a break.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.120
I'm saying this for your sake:

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.870
Think carefully, then
make the right decision.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:29.860
Yes, sir.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.990
Jeez, I'm not gonna study
for any more tests!

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.260
You've worked hard at your studies.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.140
If I hadn't, I couldn't go
to the same place as you.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.940
I think the classes will be tough here.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:47.910
You're going to have to
study hard again, Daichi.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:50.270
Yeah, I know.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.700
Daichi...

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.670
You've gotten into high school,
but what'll you do now?

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:07.350
Me? I'm gonna enjoy the
springtime of our lives!

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.170
What about you?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.440
Me, too.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.170
Yes!

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.990
The ornament has been blown off, eh?

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.410
The Diet Building is destroyed!

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.770
Give me all of Ryumyaku.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:12.750
Understood. Ryumyaku Circuit fully open!

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.980
Don't take your eyes off his condition!

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.130
Don't worry about me.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:18.780
Just do what you all have to do.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:33.850
Now. Do it!

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.780
Cerberus. Baal.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.550
Back them up.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:06.800
Lugh. Lend me your strength.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.540
It's working. Our demons can win this!

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:16.980
Pallas Athena!

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:25.660
How's that?

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.370
What's this? What's it up to?

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:40.820
What's this frequency?

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:42.960
Massive interference with D Data!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:51.950
Hey, what's going on?

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:54.230
What do you mean, "Healing"?!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.310
The demons were forcibly returned?

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.320
Sure enough, it had
an ace up its sleeve.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.570
Acting separately was the right move.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:09.200
BeneTnasch

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:09.200
The disruption wave
destroyed our D Data.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.120
We should fight frequency
with frequency.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:18.460
Trumpeter. Neutralize
that disruption wave.

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:32.810
Fumi?

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:37.850
Yes. Trumpeter's symphony has
sealed the disruption wave.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.210
It won't fall for the same trick again.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.610
A new dead face clip has arrived.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:47.320
Fumi, get out of there!

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.230
Ah, it noticed me.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.760
I might not make it.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.970
And after I've come so far...

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.800
I'm bummed I can't stand
before Polaris' judgment.

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:05.280
Sakotchi, watch things for me.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:05.840
Fumi!

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:09.050
So, this is death? Huh.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.740
Damn you!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.640
My Power is healing, too?!

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:19.620
It can't be!

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:20.290
Same here.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:20.960
Oh, no!

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.200
The other demons can't go out either.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.110
Fumi may have sealed the enemy's power,

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.610
but we have to wait for
our demons to heal!

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:37.080
We can't protect them.
It's inevitable, eh?

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:40.710
Sir!

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:41.750
Fall back!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:56.640
No matter what the sacrifice,
I must not be beaten!

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:17.360
Hey! No!

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.520
It can't be...

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.620
Airi.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:44.400
Hinako?

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.650
Hinako!

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:52.320
Hinako!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:53.570
Hurry and go!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.770
Hinako! I'll soon--

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:57.540
Idiot! You gotta protect Nitta.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:02.230
That's my final request.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.190
No! Hinako!

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.130
Stand! Run!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.590
Hurry! Don't stop!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:22.300
Suzaku!

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:27.630
Byakko?

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.600
What's going on?

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.560
Hibiki.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.320
The others?

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:37.530
Hibiki. They're... They're...!

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:48.710
Hibiki?

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.450
Th-The demons got beat?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:01.830
Sir!

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:09.900
You abandoned them, didn't you?

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.150
You abandoned your comrades!

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.990
Nuisances are of no use.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:19.100
Yamato! What do you mean, nuisances?!

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:23.200
You have no qualms about using
people and tossing them aside?!

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:25.190
Why all this now?

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:28.930
I believe I told you at the start:

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.290
There is no room for mercy.

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:33.110
If there isn't, then what?!

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:36.630
To survive like that...
How is that survival?

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:38.410
What can be gained?

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:42.330
Through Polaris's power,
I will create a new order.

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.540
Then shall humanity properly thrive.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.870
But that's just YOUR
selfishly imposed order!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.200
The world is selfish as it is.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.090
Someone must change things.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.820
Don't tell me you don't
understand as such.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.450
I DON'T understand! How could I?

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:03.350
I don't want some future built
on the deaths of my friends!

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.960
Then what do you want?

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:12.590
To fix things. One more time!

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.940
Everyone's wanted to protect
the world as it is!

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.570
No matter how twisted it may be.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:21.220
We should change things by human hands!

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.210
That garbage?

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.950
If things could be changed,
they already would have been.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.020
There is no hope for the weak.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.650
That's why you want to
remake things, huh?

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.860
No!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:38.030
I'd wanted you to follow me.

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:40.050
How unfortunate.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:53.130
Hibiki!

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.300
Hurry up and heal!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:56.800
Dammit!

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.190
What the hell?

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:02.680
Why can't I help my friends
at a time like this?!

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:24.430
What?

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:26.990
Hee ho!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:34.250
Stop picking on Hibiki!

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.750
Daichi.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.740
The fairy, Jack Frost!

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:43.160
A demon above even Baal
and Pallas Athena.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.470
Shijima.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.290
Go! My demon, Jack Frost!

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.500
Hee ho!

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:06.990
Hope, huh? We've got it.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:10.330
After all, we're still alive!

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.230
That's right.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.370
Let's go back to that day.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.900
Let's do it over again.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:20.380
We can do that!

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:37.270
It's over. Septentriones.

00:21:59.570 --> 00:22:02.370
We've survived the
seven days of judgment.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.530
Humanity wins.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:09.320
No, Yamato.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.640
I'm... not letting you go.

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:16.870
Hibiki. Then kill me.

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:20.420
If you aren't prepared
to do that, then shut up.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:25.200
But if you intend to stand in my way...

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:27.140
I'll kill you.

00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:35.020
No, Yamato.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:45.000
I won't let you kill Hibiki.
